se there  were some other kids that I met who were  into that sort of stuff my friend Steve  my friend John who went to my school my  friend Keith who had gone to elementary  school with and you know we would try to  to do this role playing stuff and then I  I realized that there were other you  know extensions to this so the Dungeons  and Dragons you know you had the  beginners thing you had the advance and  as it turned out my Uncle John had some  of the even earlier Dungeons and Dragons  stuff because his brother-in-law Bill  these are down in Chicago was into this  sort of thing so I had I had him to chat  with  um and you know they they actually gave  me some of their old rule books and the  funny thing was I'm trying to make sense  of all of this and wrap my head around  it and the stuff doesn't actually map on  to each other other quite so coherently  anyway long story short I get you know  into war games a bit more my dad  unfortunately passes away in August of  1982. otherwise I think he would have  been quite interested in in you know  these things with me as well and  in a way  um  doing this kind of stuff  the fantasy you know role-playing and  the war gaming and the other things that  I was getting into was uh an escape from  the not really dealing with grief very  well and all that kind of stuff and then  you know I'd find people who are into  gaming in general and so it went on a  couple different directions like for  example my friend John he had a younger  brother Mark and they were into the  Steve Jackson game stuff with car wars  and uh ogre to a certain degree which  was this you know futuristic tank games  Car Wars is sort of like a Mad Max you  know you put guns on your cars and you  know everybody's driving between cities  and it's kind of post-apocalyptic and we  had lots and lots of fun and all of  these things were just kind of like  being churned out and I remember being  allowed to play some DND with with some  of my friends in Middle School like  during break times and of course we get  made fun of you know oh you bunch of  nerds and stuff like that but we're  we're really into it we could never get  things working all the way through like  we never really made it through an  entire module so there was the  role-playing aspect and then that led me  into other role-playing games along with  other people who I knew so you know I  bought Gamma World which was another TSR  TSR did the uh The Dungeons and Dragons  and Gamma World was somewhat compatible  with it that was a post-apocalyptic  post-nuclear apocalypse game as well and  um what else did I I got my hands on  paranoia at one time never actually got  to play it unfortunately  um and on the other hand  I was doing the other you know tabletop  war games we had a neighbor who kind of  wanted to be my surrogate dad uh Bill  Maris and and he would he had a whole  bunch of these games and he would lend  them to me some of which I kept forever  um and uh you know sometimes I'd lose  some of the counters and stuff too and  and sometimes he and I would play these  games together and that was a lot of fun  stay up late you know match wits in  Blitzkrieg or this there was a Frederick  the great the Seven Years War there was  a game called War and Peace that he lent  me that was the entire Napoleonic Wars  that I played on a massive coffee table  um just as a side note sometimes I'd get  these things set up and then my dog  would come in the room and she had that  she was a black lab German Shepherd mix  and so she had a big long bushy tail and  she'd walk by and she'd like you know  her Tails sweep all these things off  there was a World War II game called  Third Reich that I would play as well  and oftentimes I played these games  where I would take each side and I would  play against myself and so you know this  sort of thing continued on  um  you know there's Bill Maris there was uh  playing these games with the uh the two  brothers and sometimes with 