me of these these  other people  and um  you know I continued playing some of the  other games and then you know I finished  high school and went off and was in the  Army and interestingly while I was in  the Army I actually played a lot of D  and D because weirdly enough in you know  uh the unit that I was in there were a  lot of guys who were into that and it  was it was okay there were a lot of  people who were what we call rules  lawyers where they're always trying to  like you know argue about stuff or they  were trying to maximize their stats or  their their playing their I think there  were a lot of guys who were like  indulging their feminine side because  they'd roll themselves up some you know  female uh half elf and then you know  basically she would sleep with the other  non-player characters and stuff like  that  um but you know it was It was kind of  fun and then I I get out of the army and  I I knew this guy Bill who lived in  Wauwatosa which is you know close that's  in the Milwaukee area and he and his his  friends all these 20-somethings they  were into role-playing games as well uh  in particular Twilight 2000 which then  um you know somebody who'd been in the  military  uh I I was sort of a natural for that so  they he would come out and pick me up  and Waukesha which we were living in by  then we'd move from Wales to Waukesha  and I'd come out and hang out with him  and his brother and all these other  friends and we'd play Twilight 2000 and  occasionally other games as well so you  know  there were a lot of uh people to do  interesting things but then I went up to  college and there were some people who  were into gaming up there as well and we  we played Twilight 2000 we actually  adapted it to some sort of zombie  scenario and I made up a whole bunch of  stuff I was gm'ing by then  um and and there were some other people  who were into doing the the board games  as well I I got to play squad leader  with with a few people and  um you know tha