ot of fun and so I think  that's pretty cool so maybe that's where  I'll well there's one other thing I'll  tell you about before I end the story so  there's there's a book out there that's  hard to get your hands on although there  is a PDF floating around on the internet  and it's called Fantasy war gaming and  you got to remember that in the 1980s  all these different companies all these  different people were putting out game  systems some of which uh were quite  successful think about Dungeons and  Dragons some of which were pretty cool  but never lived up to their full  potential and didn't get the traction  that they wanted some of which tried to  do a little bit of everything you think  about gurps you know the generic  Universal role-playing game which I also  did with Bill and his brother and some  of these other people now that I recall  and this Fantasy war gaming was was an  attempt to try to make it very  historical it was a it was in one book  never got to play it with anybody but  the the rule system to me looked pretty  cool and I would spend hours reading  through this book I even remember like  taking it on Spring Break  um  it got very little love from other  Gamers as a matter of fact if you go  online and look it up people say it's  one of the worst systems ever developed  you know but I actually thought it was  pretty cool and I think that you know  there's probably a lot of other things  out there like that where  um you know some people will criticize  it but others will say ah there's  there's something kind of kind of neat  here  um and so  you know I haven't thought about these  things for quite a long time but I was  spurred to Again by my colleague posting  uh the Steve Jackson games that I got to  play to some degree but not as much as I  would have liked and uh I think it's  kind of cool that that nowadays if  you're into that sort of stuff  um you know it's it's become part of Pop  Culture think about stranger things  right or other 